    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe trtllm_mla backend allocates its workspace once at startup from a\nhardcoded `DEFAULT_WORKSPACE_SIZE_MB = 150`. flashinfer's trtllm-gen\nkernel carves the prefill softmax stats out of this workspace only when\nLSE is requested, sized\n`8 B (float2) x num_qo_heads x batch_size x round_up(max_q_len, 256) + 1 MB guard`\n(see `trtllm_fmha_kernel_launcher.cu`). The demand therefore grows with\nthe prefill batch shape: a 64K-token chunked-prefill batch needs\n**183,795,712 B (~175 MB)** and the scheduler process aborts with:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: flashinfer allocator.h:71 Buffer overflow\n  allocating trtllm_gen_softmax_workspace with size 183795712\n```\n\nAt the common 16K chunk size the demand is ~44 MB\n(8 B x heads x small batch x round_up(16384, 256)), so the fixed size\nnever surfaced before. This affects any trtllm_mla deployment with a\nlarge chunked-prefill-size — PD disaggregation is not required.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- **Register `SGLANG_TRTLLM_WORKSPACE_MB`** (environ.py, next to\n  `SGLANG_FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_SIZE`) and read it at allocation time;\n  unset keeps the 150 MB default, so existing deployments are unchanged.\n- **Document the variable** in `docs/references/environment_variables.mdx`\n  with the sizing guidance.\n\nThe default intentionally stays at 150 MB: raising it for everyone would\nadd a few hundred MB of permanently-allocated memory per GPU for users\nwho never hit the ceiling, while large-chunk deployments get an explicit,\ndocumented knob. Deployments running chunked-prefill-size >= 32768 should\nset e.g. `SGLANG_TRTLLM_WORKSPACE_MB=512`.\n\nNote on decode: recent main work lets decode also request LSE, but decode\ndemand stays tiny (max_q_len = 1 per request — a few KB per batch), so\nthe 150 MB default covers it with orders of magnitude of headroom.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe change only resizes a scratch buffer at startup; kernel inputs and\noutputs are untouched. Production validation: full-model (93-layer\nKimi-K3) PD+DCP rounds at chunk 65536 (2x 30-min, c32, 2,436 requests, 0\nerrors, 0 transfer failures) ran with the workspace raised via this env\nto 512 MB — the configuration that previously died on the first\n64K-token batch — plus a 12-question gsm8k probe afterwards (acc=1.000,\ninvalid=0.000). The env plumbing was verified end to end: the variable is\nregistered in environ.py and the running server reports the configured\nvalue.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo runtime path added: the allocation happens once at startup. Decode and\nsmall-prefill deployments keep the exact upstream behavior.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit guide\n      (pre-commit passes on all touched files).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests guide\n      (env plumbing only; validated in production-shaped runs, see above).\n- [x] Update documentation according to the Write documentations guide\n      (environment_variables.mdx entry added).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results (see sections above).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38213794675](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38213794675)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38213793852](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38213793852)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38213793935](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38213793935)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
